I walked towards the fruit shops.
There were many fresh pineapples there.
A vendor looked at me and smiled.
He cut a small piece of pineapple.
He gave it to me on the tip of the knife.
I took that piece.
I ate it.
It was very sweet.
I did not ask the price.
The vendor quickly said the price.
"One pineapple is sixty rupees," he said.
I liked it.
"I want one pineapple," I said.
He took a big pineapple.
He gave it to me.
I gave sixty rupees.
I said thank you to the vendor.
I walked forward.
